{"name":"Blue Raspberry Seed","hex":"#3aa2c6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"raspberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant Rubus idaeus.","Any of many other (but not all) species in the genus Rubus."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor/flavour of raspberries.","Of a dark pinkish red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raspberry"},{"term":"seed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any propagative portion of a plant which may be sown, such as true seeds, seed-like fruits, tubers, or bulbs.","A fertilized and ripened ovule, containing an embryonic plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To plant or sow an area with seeds.","To shed seeds (refers to plants)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raspberry","blocks":[{"text":"The raspberry is the edible fruit of several plant species in the genus Rubus of the rose family, most of which are in the subgenus Idaeobatus. The name also applies to these plants themselves. Raspberries are perennial with woody stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry","wikidata":"Q13179"},{"title":"Seed","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a seed is a plant structure containing an embryo and stored nutrients in a protective coat called a testa. More generally, the term seed means anything that can be sown, which may include seed and husk or tuber. Seeds are the product of the ripened ovule, after the embryo sac is fertilized by sperm from pollen, forming a zygote. The embryo within a seed develops from the zygote and grows within the mother plant to a certain size before growth is halted."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/%D0%A0%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B5_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%8F%D0%BD.jpg/330px-%D0%A0%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B5_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%8F%D0%BD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seed","wikidata":"Q40763"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"},{"title":"Raspberry (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Raspberry is a color that resembles the color of raspberries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Raspberry_-_whole_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_whole_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry_(color)","wikidata":"Q3080423"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalved_blackberry_(Rubus_fruticosus)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/500px-Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/1280px-Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/500px-Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red-fruited raspberries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaspberries_(Rubus_idaeus).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Fert%C5%91di_k%C3%A1rmin_m%C3%A1lna.JPG/500px-Fert%C5%91di_k%C3%A1rmin_m%C3%A1lna.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1